@*
    UI-SPEC §Color semantic status table — status chip colors:
      OK / Active / Healthy / Online  → .chip.healthy   (green-bg, green dot)
      Degraded                        → .chip.degraded  (amber-bg, amber dot)
      Down / Error / Banned           → .chip.down      (red-bg, red dot)
      InMatch / In match / In-match   → .chip.in-match  (amber-bg, amber dot)        [Phase 6 / Plan 06-07]
      Offline                         → .chip.offline   (neutral surface-2, fg-3 dot) [Phase 6 / Plan 06-07]
      (anything else)                 → .chip.info      (blue-bg, blue dot)

    role="status" + aria-label mirrors UI-SPEC §Interaction Contract accessibility rule
    ("Status chips: role=\"status\" + aria-label=\"{status text}\"").

    Plan 03.1-08 — re-skinned: replaced <MudChip> with sketch's <span class="chip"> + dot
    indicator from gamekit-admin.css (.chip / .chip.healthy / .chip.degraded / .chip.down /
    .chip.info rules already ported from sketch styles.css in Plan 02).

    Plan 06-07 — Phase 6 Presence panel precedence change (06-PATTERNS Critical Misuse
    Warning #10 + UI-SPEC §5): the literal status "offline" used to resolve to the red
    .chip.down class alongside "down"/"error"/"banned". UI-SPEC §5 wants "offline" rendered
    in neutral gray (the player is not currently online but is not a problem state). The
    "down"/"offline"/"error"/"banned" arm has been SPLIT into two arms so "offline" now
    maps to the new neutral .chip.offline class while "down"/"error"/"banned" continue to
    resolve to the red .chip.down class (banned-user chips on Admins.razor / Players.razor
    do NOT regress). Two new arms were added: "inmatch"/"in match"/"in-match" → .chip.in-match
    (amber) and "offline" → .chip.offline (neutral). The new "offline" arm is placed BEFORE
    the existing "down"/"error"/"banned" arm because C# switch arms are evaluated top-to-bottom
    and we want the new precedence to win.
*@
<span class="chip @ChipModifierClass(Status)" role="status" aria-label="@Status">
    <span class="dot"></span>
    @Status
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>The status text to display. Drives both the chip label and the color mapping.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Status { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Maps a status string to the sketch's <c>.chip.{modifier}</c> class per the UI-SPEC
    /// §Color semantic-status allowlist. Unknown values default to <c>.chip.info</c>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="status">Status string (case-insensitive).</param>
    /// <returns>Modifier class name appended after the base <c>.chip</c>.</returns>
    private static string ChipModifierClass(string status) => status?.Trim().ToLowerInvariant() switch
    {
        "ok" or "active" or "healthy" or "online" or "up" => "healthy",
        "degraded" or "warning" => "degraded",
        "inmatch" or "in match" or "in-match" => "in-match",
        "offline" => "offline",
        "down" or "error" or "banned" => "down",
        _ => "info",
    };
}
